course: dictionary
lesson: 13925
title: Leftovers and leftover
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Leftovers are food that was not eaten at a meal and is kept to eat later. «We put the leftovers in the fridge for lunch tomorrow.» The word leftovers is nearly always used for food, and it is plural, so we say leftovers, not leftover, when we mean the food.
explain: Leftover is an adjective, a describing word. It means remaining after the rest has been used. «Dad made leftover pizza for supper.» The pizza is describing the kind of pizza: pizza that was left from earlier. «There is some leftover paint in the shed» means paint that is left after the painting is done.
explain: Look at the words around leftover to work out its meaning. If the sentence is about food, paint, money or numbers, the word is telling you that something is still there, after the rest has been used. A quick check is to put the words «what is left over» in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Leftovers are food that is not eaten at a meal and is kept for later.
fact: Leftover is an adjective that means remaining after the rest has been used.
fact: «Leftover» can describe food, paint or money: «leftover pizza», «leftover paint», «leftover money».
fact: In maths, a leftover is the amount that remains after you share or divide, like the remainder.
fact: Food safety tip: leftovers should be cooled quickly, covered, kept cold, eaten within a day or two, and reheated until piping hot.
exercise: «We put the leftovers in the fridge for tomorrow.» What are leftovers? | Plates and cups that need washing | *Food that was not eaten at a meal and is kept to eat later | Cold drinks sold at a shop | Food that is still cooking on the stove
exercise: Dad says, «There is some leftover paint in the shed.» What does leftover mean here? | Painted on a wall | *Remaining after the rest has been used | Wet and sticky | Brand new and never opened
exercise: Share 17 sweets into groups of 5. You get 3 groups and 2 sweets are left over. What is the leftover amount? | 3 | 17 | *2 | 5
test: Leftover pizza should be eaten within a day or two. How long should you keep leftovers before eating them? | A week | A month | Until next summer | *Within a day or two
test: Mum put the ___ soup in a covered bowl in the fridge. Which word fits best? | curious | *leftover | ancient | barely
exam: Before you eat leftovers, what should you do to make them safe? | Leave them out on the side all night | Eat them after a week | *Reheat them until piping hot | Mix them with paint
